  "$Comment": "Tomas's Christmas Loaf, Tomas the Miller's own dish and his secret: a sweet loaf baked two at a time at a Chef's Stove (the Cookingbench, its Baked tab) once a player has learned it from Christmas_Recipe_Tomas_Loaf, which his stall sells to a player holding either key to his secret (his apprentice quest, or Crafting level 20 on a server running MMO Skill Tree). It wears the game's bread (Food_Bread's model, texture and icon). Eating one gives an instant heal, the cookie's Christmas_Food_Speed and the cocoa's Christmas_Food_Warmth (not its health regen), and nothing a Christmas Cake does not give, so the secret is a new dish, never more power. Its description in items.lang writes the numbers out: change it with the effects. Recipe.Input is what one batch costs, Recipe.Output and OutputQuantity how many it makes (keep the two equal); Fuel is the 3 fuel every baked dish in the game burns. The loaf is good all year.",
